{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792445509,"nonce":"YQX1nrORwrH8OGXOs3YGgnRQy1g=","message":"Inactive tabs, measured with footprint from outside (a harness of ten or twenty editors in one tree, hidden):\n\n**Steady cost and high-water mark are different things.** Measured as growth between batches once the heap has settled, an element costs about 6 KB for a plain div, 9 KB with a class, 15 KB for a Text, and about 60 KB for anything styled by `.ui-button`. The first batches cost several times that, because building makes garbage between the objects it keeps and the heap does not give the pages back; later allocations reuse them. So a hidden tab's footprint is the steady cost (4 to 5 MB for a short file, 5 MB more for 2,800 lines, a few MB for the minimap) on top of a high-water mark that the building left, and that is what stays high and falls slowly.\n\n**What a hidden editor holds:** 408 (short file) to 530 (120 KB) styled elements, 46 row slots each in RayDE; per slot a line div, token texts, a gutter div, a marker slot and its dot, a line number, a fold slot, a fold control with an svg. The gutter is about half of the steady cost.\n\n**`.ui-button` costs 50 to 80 KB for each element it styles** (a plain div with only that class, no component code, costs the same; an Interaction is 3 to 6 KB). It is the stylesheet: six transitions, hover, active and focus-visible rules (a state signal and a watch each), shadows and outline. The editor's fold control was a Button for every row slot; it is a plain element now, and twenty hidden editors hold 25 MB less (308 to 283 MB, three runs each).\n\n**RayDE (6 tabs): 9,371 styled elements**, 4,590 of them with no class, 1,493 code tokens and numbers, 454 icons, 856 command-palette items and labels: the palette builds a row for every file and command while it is closed (428 elements), which is the biggest single block outside the editors.\n\n**Time to build is mostly native:** building thousands of elements spends 37% in `LayoutTree.flush` and 37% in the cascade's restyle, in std SipHash lookups (`HashMap\u003cNodeId, LayoutNodeId\u003e`, `HashMap\u003cu64, Element\u003e`) and a linear `find_map` over children; a faster hasher in blinc_layout and blinc_abi would shorten every tab open.\n\nNext: the palette builds rows only when opened (RayDE); the minimap and slots of a hidden editor, and an editor never shown, building nothing until it is measured.","files":null}]}